# 23. Project Limitations

- Fraud predictions are probabilistic and cannot guarantee detection of every fraudulent transaction.
- Public datasets may not fully represent home decor e-commerce behavior.
- Synthetic transactions will supplement public training data.
- Payment integrations may initially use sandbox/test mode.
- Some device and IP intelligence features depend on available, lawful data collection.
- The platform will provide fraud risk assessment and decision support rather than claim to establish criminal intent.

# 24. Expected Outcome

FraudShield AI will provide a unified platform through which merchants can operate online stores and monitor suspicious transactions using machine learning.

The project will demonstrate the practical application of full-stack development, SaaS architecture, relational database design, machine learning, anomaly detection, explainable AI and secure transaction processing.

The final system will be a deployable web application suitable for an academic demonstration and further commercial development.